findings.body:
The class-level @MainActor is removed from EditBookmarkViewModelTests, but EditBookmarkViewModel.selectFolder is declared @MainActor (lines 81-82 of EditBookmarkViewModel.swift). The synchronous test methods such as testSelectFolder_callsOnFolderStatusUpdate call it from a nonisolated context. Under Swift 6 this is an error, and under Swift 5 with strict concurrency it is a warning. Either way it is an actor-isolation diagnostic in the area this PR is meant to clean up.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/ClientTests/Library/Bookmarks/EditBookmarkViewModelTests.swift" lines="11-11"}

::callout{type="warning"}
EditBookmarkDataSourceTests and StoriesFeedDiffableDataSourceTests keep @MainActor on the class, so this is inconsistent. Restoring the annotation is also compatible with the new async setUp/tearDown.

testRequestAuthorization changes XCTAssertTrue to Swift assert(...). A failing assert traps the whole test process, which aborts the test run instead of recording a failure for this test. In optimized builds, assert compiles to nothing, so the check disappears.

The mock completes synchronously, so the closure does run, but the test has no clean failure path. The [center] capture is also unnecessary, because the callback fires before the test returns.

NotificationManager already has an async throws requestAuthorization() overload, which removes the callback entirely.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/ClientTests/Helpers/NotificationManagerTests.swift" lines="26-29"}

